RLK
---

Minimal C99 library for 2D grid-based games and roguelikes.

Build:
  make                  # Build librlk.a
  make lint             # Static analysis (-Werror)
  make test             # Run unit tests
  make clean            # Remove build artifacts

Note: the Makefiles use BSD make. On Linux, use `bmake` or `pmake`
instead of GNU make.

Configuration:
  Copy config.mk.example to config.mk to customize CFLAGS or library paths.

Design:
  - Zero allocation: the lib never calls malloc/free; all buffers are
    caller-owned (doc/architecture.md, "Memory model").
  - Determinism: same seed + same build -> identical world, byte for byte
    (build flags enforced in Makefile.inc).

Documentation:
  doc/architecture.md   # Layered architecture, memory model, determinism contract
  doc/conventions.md    # Naming rules

Headers:
  rlk.h                # Umbrella header (includes all of the below)
  err.h                # Error handling
  hash.h               # Seed/coordinate hashing
  fmath.h              # Math helpers
  noise.h              # Noise generation (value, perlin, fbm)
  rng.h                # Deterministic PRNG (splitmix64)
  geom.h               # Rect (region) + lattice (grid geometry on world)
  grid.h               # Coarse float grid with bilinear sampling
  tilemap.h            # 2D grid with occupancy
  wg_nf.h              # Noise-field world generation
  wg_nf_modulator.h    # Voronoi modulation stage for wg_nf
  wg_nf_grid.h         # Sample a coarse grid into wg_nf fields
  wg_nf_flow.h         # Read flow data into wg_nf fields
  wg_nf_rivers.h       # Project wg_flow drainage into per-tile river masks
  wg_nf_relief.h       # Standardised elevation (domain warp, fjords, lapse)
  wg_nf_poi.h          # Detect Points of Interest during wg_nf fill
  wg_flow.h            # Hydrology on a coarse grid: pits, D8 drainage, accumulation
  wg_poi.h             # Points of interest (fixed-capacity list, no allocation)
  wg_ca.h              # Cellular Automata (caves, organic structures)
  wg_bsp.h             # Binary Space Partitioning (rooms + corridors)

Demos:
  demo/demo_tilemap_viewer.c  # Interactive terrain viewer (PXL)

